      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    t = int(data[0])\n    index = 1\n    results = []\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(data[index]); index += 1\n        a = list(map(int, data[index:index+n]))\n        index += n\n        \n        # Count frequency of each exponent value\n        freq = Counter(a)\n        \n        # Count pairs (i, j) with i < j such that b_i^b_j = b_j^b_i\n        # b_i = 2^a_i, b_j = 2^a_j\n        # Condition: (2^a_i)^(2^a_j) = (2^a_j)^(2^a_i)\n        # Simplifies to: 2^(a_i * 2^a_j) = 2^(a_j * 2^a_i)\n        # So: a_i * 2^a_j = a_j * 2^a_i\n        # This holds when a_i = a_j or {a_i, a_j} = {1, 2}\n        \n        count = 0\n        \n        # Same exponents: C(freq[x], 2) for each x\n        for x in freq:\n            count += freq[x] * (freq[x] - 1) // 2\n        \n        # Special case: pairs (1, 2) and (2, 1)\n        if 1 in freq and 2 in freq:\n            count += freq[1] * freq[2]\n            \n        results.append(str(count))\n    \n    print('\\n'.join(results))\n\nsolve()\n```",
