      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longestValidSubstring(word: str, forbidden: list) -> int:\n    forbidden_set = set(forbidden)\n    n = len(word)\n    max_len = 0\n    left = 0\n    \n    for right in range(n):\n        # Check all substrings ending at 'right' starting from current 'left'\n        for start in range(left, right + 1):\n            substr = word[start:right + 1]\n            # Since forbidden[i] length <= 10, we can break early if substr length > 10\n            if len(substr) > 10:\n                break\n            if substr in forbidden_set:\n                left = start + 1  # Move left bound past the invalid substring\n                break\n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return max_len\n```",
