      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    import bisect\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Read W, H\n    W = int(data[0])\n    H = int(data[1])\n    idx = 2\n    \n    # Read N and strawberries\n    N = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n    strawberries = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        p = int(data[idx]); q = int(data[idx+1]); idx += 2\n        strawberries.append((p, q))\n    \n    # Read A and vertical cuts\n    A = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n    a_cuts = list(map(int, data[idx:idx+A])); idx += A\n    \n    # Read B and horizontal cuts\n    B = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n    b_cuts = list(map(int, data[idx:idx+B])); idx += B\n    \n    # Add boundaries to define regions\n    a_regions = [0] + a_cuts + [W]\n    b_regions = [0] + b_cuts + [H]\n    \n    # Count strawberries in each region\n    counts = [[0] * B for _ in range(A)]\n    \n    for p, q in strawberries:\n        i = bisect.bisect_left(a_regions, p) - 1\n        j = bisect.bisect_left(b_regions, q) - 1\n        if i < A and j < B:\n            counts[i][j] += 1\n    \n    all_vals = [count for row in counts for count in row]\n    m = min(all_vals)\n    M = max(all_vals)\n    \n    print(m, M)\n\nsolve()\n```",
