    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    from collections import deque\n    \n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    H, W = int(data[0]), int(data[1])\n    grid = [list(data[i+2]) for i in range(H)]\n    \n    # Use a set to track currently active positions\n    active = set((i, j) for i in range(H) for j in range(W))\n    \n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        changed = False\n        marked = set()\n        \n        # Row processing\n        for i in range(H):\n            row_active = [(j, grid[i][j]) for j in range(W) if (i, j) in active]\n            if len(row_active) < 2:\n                continue\n            colors = [color for _, color in row_active]\n            if len(set(colors)) == 1:\n                marked.update((i, j) for j, _ in row_active)\n        \n        # Column processing\n        for j in range(W):\n            col_active = [(i, grid[i][j]) for i in range(H) if (i, j) in active]\n            if len(col_active) < 2:\n                continue\n            colors = [color for _, color in col_active]\n            if len(set(colors)) == 1:\n                marked.update((i, j) for i, _ in col_active)\n        \n        if marked:\n            active -= marked\n            changed = True\n    \n    print(len(active))\n\nsolve()\n```",
