      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longestSpecialSubstring(s: str) -> int:\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    \n    # Dictionary to store frequency of each special substring\n    freq = defaultdict(int)\n    \n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # Generate all possible substrings\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n + 1):\n            substring = s[i:j]\n            # Check if the substring is special (all same characters)\n            if len(set(substring)) == 1:\n                freq[substring] += 1\n    \n    max_length = -1\n    \n    # Find the longest special substring occurring at least thrice\n    for substr, count in freq.items():\n        if count >= 3:\n            max_length = max(max_length, len(substr))\n    \n    return max_length\n```",
