      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve(wordsContainer, wordsQuery):\n    def get_suffix(s, k):\n        return s[-k:] if k <= len(s) else \"\"\n    \n    n = len(wordsContainer)\n    ans = []\n    \n    # Precompute reversed strings for faster suffix matching\n    rev_container = [s[::-1] for s in wordsContainer]\n    \n    for query in wordsQuery:\n        rev_query = query[::-1]\n        max_suffix_len = 0\n        best_idx = 0\n        \n        # Try all possible suffix lengths from longest to shortest\n        for i in range(n):\n            container_word = rev_container[i]\n            min_len = min(len(container_word), len(rev_query))\n            common_len = 0\n            \n            # Check how many characters match from the start (which is suffix in original)\n            for j in range(min_len):\n                if container_word[j] == rev_query[j]:\n                    common_len += 1\n                else:\n                    break\n            \n            if common_len > max_suffix_len:\n                max_suffix_len = common_len\n                best_idx = i\n            elif common_len == max_suffix_len and common_len > 0:\n                # Tie-breaking: smallest length first, then earliest occurrence\n                if len(wordsContainer[i]) < len(wordsContainer[best_idx]):\n                    best_idx = i\n                # If same length, keep the one with smaller index (earlier occurrence)\n        \n        # If no suffix matched, we need to choose based on shortest length and earliest occurrence\n        if max_suffix_len == 0:\n            best_idx = 0\n            for i in range(1, n):\n                if len(wordsContainer[i]) < len(wordsContainer[best_idx]):\n                    best_idx = i\n        \n        ans.append(best_idx)\n    \n    return ans\n```",
