    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    A = list(map(int, data[1:]))\n    \n    # Directed graph: i-th edge goes from vertex (i+1) to A[i]\n    # We need to find a directed cycle\n    \n    visited = [False] * (n + 1)\n    \n    for start in range(1, n + 1):\n        if visited[start]:\n            continue\n            \n        path = []\n        current = start\n        \n        # Follow the path until we meet a visited node\n        while not visited[current]:\n            visited[current] = True\n            path.append(current)\n            current = A[current - 1]  # A is 0-indexed, current is 1-indexed\n        \n        # If current is in path, we found a cycle\n        if current in path:\n            idx = path.index(current)\n            cycle = path[idx:]\n            m = len(cycle)\n            print(m)\n            print(' '.join(map(str, cycle)))\n            return\n\nsolve()\n```",
