    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    bases = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        w, x = map(int, data[i].split())\n        bases.append((w, x))\n    \n    # For each base, the meeting time in UTC must be [t, t+1) such that local time [x+t mod 24, x+t+1 mod 24] is within [9, 18]\n    # So 9 <= x + t mod 24 < 17 (since meeting is 1 hour, end time < 18 => start time < 17)\n    \n    max_employees = 0\n    \n    # Try all possible meeting start times in UTC: from 0 to 23\n    for t in range(24):\n        total = 0\n        for w, x in bases:\n            # Calculate local meeting start time\n            local_start = (x + t) % 24\n            # Check if [local_start, local_start + 1) is fully within [9, 18)\n            if local_start >= 9 and local_start + 1 <= 18:\n                total += w\n        if total > max_employees:\n            max_employees = total\n    \n    print(max_employees)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
