      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque, defaultdict\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split('\\n')\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n, m = map(int, data[0].split())\n    edges = []\n    graph = [[] for _ in range(n+1)]\n    \n    for i in range(1, m+1):\n        u, v, b, c = map(int, data[i].split())\n        edges.append((u, v, b, c))\n        graph[u].append(i-1)\n    \n    # Binary search for max ratio r such that there exists path with (sum b - r*sum c) >= 0\n    low, high = 0.0, 1e9\n    \n    for _ in range(100):  # enough iterations for precision\n        mid = (low + high) / 2\n        # Compute max sum (b - mid*c) from 1 to n using DP (since DAG, topological order by vertex index)\n        dist = [-1e18] * (n+1)\n        dist[1] = 0.0\n        \n        for u in range(1, n):\n            if dist[u] == -1e18:\n                continue\n            for idx in graph[u]:\n                _, v, b, c = edges[idx]\n                new_val = dist[u] + b - mid * c\n                if new_val > dist[v]:\n                    dist[v] = new_val\n        \n        if dist[n] >= 0:\n            low = mid\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    \n    print(\"{:.15f}\".format(low))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
