    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nimport heapq\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    index = 2\n    graph = defaultdict(list)\n    \n    for _ in range(m):\n        u = int(data[index]) - 1\n        v = int(data[index + 1]) - 1\n        index += 2\n        graph[u].append(v)\n        graph[v].append(u)\n    \n    weights = list(map(int, data[index:index + n]))\n    index += n\n    counts = list(map(int, data[index:index + n]))\n    \n    total_operations = 0\n    heap = []\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        if counts[i] > 0:\n            heapq.heappush(heap, (-weights[i], i))\n    \n    while heap:\n        neg_weight, x = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        weight_x = -neg_weight\n        \n        if counts[x] == 0:\n            continue\n            \n        total_operations += 1\n        counts[x] -= 1\n        \n        neighbors = graph[x]\n        total_neighbor_weight = 0\n        valid_neighbors = []\n        \n        for y in neighbors:\n            if counts[y] < float('inf'):  # Still active\n                total_neighbor_weight += weights[y]\n                valid_neighbors.append(y)\n        \n        if total_neighbor_weight < weight_x:\n            for y in valid_neighbors:\n                counts[y] += 1\n                heapq.heappush(heap, (-weights[y], y))\n    \n    print(total_operations)\n\nmain()\n```",
