    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    import heapq\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    prices = list(map(int, data[2:2+n]))\n    L = list(map(int, data[2+n:2+n+m]))\n    D = list(map(int, data[2+n+m:2+n+2*m]))\n    \n    # Create coupons list and sort by discount descending to prioritize higher discounts\n    coupons = sorted([(L[i], D[i]) for i in range(m)], key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n    \n    # Sort items by price ascending - we want to try to apply discounts to more expensive items\n    prices.sort(reverse=True)  # We'll process from highest price\n    \n    total_cost = sum(prices)\n    # For each coupon, try to apply it to an eligible item with highest price that benefits most\n    used_coupons = [False] * m\n    savings = 0\n    \n    # For each item in descending order of price\n    for p in prices:\n        best_saving_coupon_idx = -1\n        best_saving = 0\n        \n        # Find the best coupon that can be applied (highest discount among eligible ones)\n        for j in range(m):\n            if not used_coupons[j] and coupons[j][0] <= p:  # eligible\n                if coupons[j][1] > best_saving:\n                    best_saving = coupons[j][1]\n                    best_saving_coupon_idx = j\n        \n        if best_saving_coupon_idx != -1:\n            savings += best_saving\n            used_coupons[best_saving_coupon_idx] = True\n    \n    print(total_cost - savings)\n\nmain()\n```",
