      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    cards = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = int(data[1 + 2*i])\n        c = int(data[2 + 2*i])\n        cards.append((a, c, i+1))\n    \n    # Sort by strength descending, cost ascending to process efficiently\n    cards.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[0], x[1]))\n    \n    # Keep cards where no previous card has higher strength but lower cost\n    result = []\n    min_cost = float('inf')\n    \n    for a, c, idx in cards:\n        if c < min_cost:\n            result.append(idx)\n            min_cost = c\n    \n    # Reverse to get ascending order by index\n    result.sort()\n    print(len(result))\n    print(*result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
