      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    L = int(data[0])\n    R = int(data[1])\n    \n    def highest_power_of_two_dividing(x):\n        if x == 0:\n            return 60  # since R <= 2^60, we can assume max power is 60\n        return (x & -x).bit_length() - 1\n\n    result = []\n    current = L\n    while current < R:\n        power = highest_power_of_two_dividing(current)\n        next_start = current + (1 << power)\n        if next_start > R:\n            next_start = R\n        result.append((current, next_start))\n        current = next_start\n    \n    print(len(result))\n    for l, r in result:\n        print(l, r)\n\nsolve()\n```",
