    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_405",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nThere is a grid of H rows and W columns, each cell having a side length of 1, and we have N tiles.\nThe i-th tile (1\\leq i\\leq N) is a rectangle of size A_i\\times B_i.\nDetermine whether it is possible to place the tiles on the grid so that all of the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- Every cell is covered by exactly one tile.\n- It is fine to have unused tiles.\n- The tiles may be rotated or flipped when placed. However, each tile must be aligned with the edges of the cells without extending outside the grid.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN H W\nA_1 B_1\nA_2 B_2\n\\ldots\nA_N B_N\n\nOutput\n\nIf it is possible to place the tiles on the grid so that all of the conditions in the problem statement are satisfied, print Yes; otherwise, print No.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1\\leq N\\leq 7\n- 1 \\leq H,W \\leq 10\n- 1\\leq A_i,B_i\\leq 10\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n5 5 5\n1 1\n3 3\n4 4\n2 3\n2 5\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\n\nPlacing the 2-nd, 4-th, and 5-th tiles as shown below covers every cell of the grid by exactly one tile.\n\nHence, print Yes.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n1 1 2\n2 3\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\n\nIt is impossible to place the tile without letting it extend outside the grid.\nHence, print No.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n1 2 2\n1 1\n\nSample Output 3\n\nNo\n\nIt is impossible to cover all cells with the tile.\nHence, print No.\n\nSample Input 4\n\n5 3 3\n1 1\n2 2\n2 2\n2 2\n2 2\n\nSample Output 4\n\nNo\n\nNote that each cell must be covered by exactly one tile.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    from itertools import permutations\n    \n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    h = int(data[1])\n    w = int(data[2])\n    \n    tiles = []\n    idx = 3\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = int(data[idx]); b = int(data[idx+1]); idx += 2\n        tiles.append((a, b))\n    \n    # Check total area first\n    grid_area = h * w\n    # Try all subsets and arrangements\n    def can_cover():\n        # Try all subsets of tiles (using bit masks)\n        for mask in range(1, 1 << n):\n            area = 0\n            used_tiles = []\n            for i in range(n):\n                if mask & (1 << i):\n                    a, b = tiles[i]\n                    # Consider both orientations\n                    area += a * b\n                    used_tiles.append(tiles[i])\n            \n            if area != grid_area:\n                continue\n            \n            # Try all permutations of used tiles\n            for perm in set(permutations(used_tiles)):\n                # Try to pack into h x w grid using simple backtracking\n                grid = [[False] * w for _ in range(h)]\n                \n                def place_tile(tile_idx, row=0, col=0):\n                    if tile_idx == len(perm):\n                        return True\n                    \n                    a, b = perm[tile_idx]\n                    # Try both orientations\n                    orientations = [(a, b), (b, a)]\n                    \n                    for orient_a, orient_b in orientations:\n                        # Find first empty cell\n                        start_r, start_c = -1, -1\n                        found = False\n                        for r in range(h):\n                            if found: break\n                            for c in range(w):\n                                if not grid[r][c]:\n                                    start_r, start_c = r, c\n                                    found = True\n                                    break\n                        \n                        if start_r == -1:\n                            return True  # Grid full but not all tiles placed? Shouldn't happen if area matches\n                        \n                        # Check if tile fits starting at (start_r, start_c)\n                        can_place = True\n                        for dr in range(orient_a):\n                            for dc in range(orient_b):\n                                nr, nc = start_r + dr, start_c + dc\n                                if nr >= h or nc >= w or grid[nr][nc]:\n                                    can_place = False\n                                    break\n                            if not can_place: break\n                        \n                        if can_place:\n                            # Place tile\n                            for dr in range(orient_a):\n                                for dc in range(orient_b):\n                                    grid[start_r + dr][start_c + dc] = True\n                            \n                            if place_tile(tile_idx + 1):\n                                return True\n                            \n                            # Undo placement\n                            for dr in range(orient_a):\n                                for dc in range(orient_b):\n                                    grid[start_r + dr][start_c + dc] = False\n                    \n                    return False\n                \n                if place_tile(0):\n                    return True\n        \n        return False\n    \n    if can_cover():\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
