      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef count_intersecting_pairs():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    intervals = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        l = int(data[1 + 2*i])\n        r = int(data[1 + 2*i + 1])\n        intervals.append((l, r))\n    \n    # Count intersections: total pairs minus non-intersecting pairs\n    # Non-intersecting: i's right < j's left OR j's right < i's left\n    # Sort by left endpoint, then use binary search for right endpoints\n    \n    intervals.sort()\n    \n    # Extract right endpoints\n    rights = [r for _, r in intervals]\n    \n    # For each interval i, count how many j > i have right_j < left_i (non-overlapping)\n    from bisect import bisect_left\n    non_overlapping = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        l_i = intervals[i][0]\n        # Find number of intervals j > i with r_j < l_i\n        idx = bisect_left(rights, l_i)\n        if idx > i:\n            non_overlapping += idx - i - 1\n    \n    total_pairs = n * (n - 1) // 2\n    result = total_pairs - non_overlapping\n    print(result)\n\ncount_intersecting_pairs()\n```",
