      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef max_partitions(s: str, k: int) -> int:\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # dp[i][mask] = max partitions for s[i:] where mask is set of chars used in current prefix\n    # But due to constraints, use greedy + simulation with try-all-changes\n    \n    def count_partitions(t):\n        i = 0\n        parts = 0\n        while i < len(t):\n            seen = set()\n            j = i\n            while j < len(t) and len(seen | {t[j]}) <= k:\n                seen.add(t[j])\n                j += 1\n            parts += 1\n            i = j\n        return parts\n    \n    best = count_partitions(s)\n    \n    # Try changing each position to each possible char\n    for i in range(n):\n        orig = s[i]\n        for c in 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz':\n            if c == orig:\n                continue\n            t = s[:i] + c + s[i+1:]\n            best = max(best, count_partitions(t))\n    \n    return best\n```",
