 size either s or s-1.\n    # So total groups = sum(ceil(c/s)) for all c, and we want min total groups over s where for each c, we can partition into groups of size s or s-1.\n    # For each c, min groups = ceil(c/s). Max group size in partition is s, min is s-1 (if possible).\n    # Feasibility: need c >= ceil(c/s)*(s-1) => always true since ceil(c/s)*(s-1) <= (c/s +1)*(s-1) not straightforward.\n    # Correct approach from known solutions: try s from 1 to max_count, compute required groups per freq.\n    for s in range(1, max_count + 1):\n        total = 0\n        for c in counts:\n            # Min groups to partition c into groups of size s or s-1\n            # If s=1, groups=c\n            # If s>1, groups = ceil(c/s) if c % s != 0 else c//s, but also check if c >= groups*(s-1)\n            groups = (c + s - 1) // s\n            if groups * (s - 1) > c:\n                continue  # Not feasible\n            total += groups\n        # But need to ensure that the actual max group size across all values is s or s-1\n        # This approach isn't complete.\n    \n    # Known solution pattern: binary search on number of groups k, check feasibility\n    lo, hi = 1, len(nums)\n    while lo < hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        # Check if mid groups possible\n        # For each freq f, need to assign to some groups. Each group can have at most ceil(mid groups capacity?) \n        # Actually: with k groups total, each group size is either floor(n/k) or ceil(n/k)\n        # Let s = ceil(len(nums)/mid)\n        # For each distinct value with frequency f, must split into groups of size at most s and at least s-1\n        # Number of groups needed for this value is ceil(f / s)\n        # Sum over all values must be <= mid\n        s = (len(nums) + mid - 1) // mid\n        needed = sum((f + s - 1) // s for f in counts)\n        if needed <= mid:\n            hi = mid\n        else:\n            lo = mid + 1\n    return lo\n```",
