      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef count_repeating_substrings():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    s = data[1].strip()\n    \n    # Count contiguous segments of same characters\n    # For each segment of length k, number of distinct repeating substrings = k\n    # (e.g., \"aaa\" has substrings \"a\", \"aa\", \"aaa\")\n    total = 0\n    i = 0\n    while i < n:\n        j = i\n        while j < n and s[j] == s[i]:\n            j += 1\n        length = j - i\n        total += length  # For segment of length L, we have L distinct repeating substrings\n        i = j\n    \n    print(total)\n\ncount_repeating_substrings()\n```",
