    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Currying transforms a function with multiple arguments into a sequence of functions each with a single argument. It can be applied to any function regardless of the number of arguments or whether arguments or return values are functions. Thus, option A is correct because currying reduces functions step by step, each time taking one argument.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
