      "generated_answer": "In Chord, each node is responsible for keys that fall in the range from its predecessor to itself (exclusive of predecessor, inclusive of node if no other node covers it). The predecessor of N6 is N3, so N6 is responsible for keys from 4 to 6. However, since we ignore the node's own ID (6), the keys N6 is responsible for are those that hash to 4, 5, or 6 \u2014 but only if no other active node claims them. But the question asks for *finger table targets*, not responsible keys.\n\nThe finger table for N6 has entries for (6 + 2^(i-1)) mod 16, i=1 to 4: 7, 8, 10, 14 \u2014 all covered by N8 except 7, which may be handled by N8 or N6 depending on successor. Target keys in finger table are the keys being pointed to, not responsibility. So the target keys are 7, 8, 10, 14.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
