      "generated_answer": "The channel capacity for an AWGN channel with input power constraint $ P $ and noise variance $ N_0/2 $ is given by $ C = \\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1 + \\text{SNR}) $. Here, $ Y = X + Z $, $ Z \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0,1) $, and $ \\mathbb{E}[Y^2] \\leq 2 $. Since $ \\mathbb{E}[Z^2] = 1 $, we get $ \\mathbb{E}[X^2] \\leq 1 $. Thus, SNR = $ \\frac{P}{N} = \\frac{1}{1} = 1 $. Then $ C = \\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1 + 1) = \\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(2) = 0.5 $.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
