      "generated_answer": "We are given the recurrence:\n\nT(1) = 7  \nT(n+1) = T(n) + 3n, for n \u2265 1\n\nThis is a linear recurrence where each step adds 3n. Unrolling:\n\nT(n) = T(1) + 3(1) + 3(2) + ... + 3(n\u22121)  \n= 7 + 3 \u2211_{k=1}^{n\u22121} k  \n= 7 + 3\u00b7(n\u22121)n/2  \n= \u0398(n\u00b2)\n\nSo the order of growth is \u0398(n\u00b2).\n\n\\boxed{J}",
