      "generated_answer": "Aristotle holds that essences are not separate, independently existing forms like in Plato\u2019s theory, but are instantiated in individual substances. If all individuals of a species cease to exist, there is nothing in which the essence is embodied, so the essence ceases to exist as well\u2014though it could potentially re-emerge. Therefore, the essence is not preserved separately and depends on the existence of individuals.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
