    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A father brings his 22-year-old son to you for evaluation. Within the past 6 weeks, this formerly socially active young man has quit his job as a restaurant manager, has become withdrawn, and now spends most of his time in his room watching TV. He reports that he occasionally receives messages from aliens through the TV. Based on this information, which of the following is the most appropriate DSM-IV diagnosis\n\nOptions: \nA. Schizophrenia\nB. Paranoid Personality Disorder\nC. Brief Reactive Psychosis\nD. Bipolar Disorder\nE. Schizophreniform Disorder\nF. Antisocial Personality Disorder\nG. Dissociative Identity Disorder\nH. Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder\nI. Generalized Anxiety Disorder\nJ. Major Depressive Disorder\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
