      "generated_answer": "To test validity using an indirect truth table, assume the premises are true and the conclusion is false. The conclusion L \u2283 K is false only when L is true and K is false. With K false and L true, from (K \u00b7 L) \u2283 M, since K \u00b7 L is false, this premise is true regardless of M. For N \u2228 K to be true with K false, N must be true. Then from N \u2283 ~M, since N is true, ~M must be true, so M is false. Thus, L and N are true, K and M are false\u2014this makes all premises true and the conclusion false.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
