    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To test validity using an indirect truth table, assume the premises are true and the conclusion is false. The conclusion ~G \u2228 ~E is false only when both G and E are true. For the conclusion to be false, G = true and E = true. From E \u2283 F, if E is true, then F must be true for the premise to hold. From G \u2283 ~F, if G is true, then ~F must be true, so F must be false\u2014contradicting F = true. Since we can't satisfy all premises with a false conclusion without contradiction, the argument is valid.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
