    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Use indirect truth tables to determine whether each set of propositions is consistent. If the set is consistent, choose an option with a consistent valuation. (There may be other consistent valuations.)\nD \u2261 E\nF \u2228 D\n~E \u00b7 ~F\n\nOptions: \nA. Inconsistent\nB. Consistent. Consistent valuation when D, E, and F are true\nC. Consistent. Consistent valuation when D and E are true and F is false\nD. Consistent. Consistent valuation when D and F are true and E is false\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We analyze consistency using the given propositions:  \n1. $ D \\equiv E $ (i.e., $ D $ and $ E $ have same truth value),  \n2. $ F \\lor D $,  \n3. $ \\neg E \\cdot \\neg F $ (i.e., $ E $ and $ F $ are both false).\n\nFrom (3): $ E = \\text{false} $, $ F = \\text{false} $.  \nThen from (1): $ D \\equiv E $ \u21d2 $ D = \\text{false} $.  \nCheck (2): $ F \\lor D = \\text{false} \\lor \\text{false} = \\text{false} $ \u2014 violates (2).  \nSo assuming (3) leads to contradiction \u2192 the set is **inconsistent**.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
