      "generated_answer": "In the event of bankruptcy, creditors are paid first, followed by preferred stockholders, and then common stockholders. Bonds are debt obligations, so bondholders have the highest claim. Therefore, the correct order is bondholders, preferred stockholders, then common stockholders.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
