    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_216",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Two power line construction routes are being considered. Route A is 15 miles long and goes around a lake. Each mile will cost $6,000 to build and $2,000 a year to maintain. At the end of fifteen years, each mile will have a salvage value of $3,000. Route B is an underwater line that cuts 5 miles across the lake. Construction costs will be $31,000 per mile and annual maintenance costs, $400 per mile. The salvage value at the end of fifteen years will be $6,000 per mile. Assuming interest is 8% and taxes are 3% of the construction costs of each power line, compare the annual costs of Route A and Route B for the first year.\n\nOptions: \nA. $41,558 for Route A and $23,654 for Route B\nB. $45,000 for Route A and $30,000 for Route B\nC. $100,000 for Route A and $50,000 for Route B\nD. $40,000 for Route A and $20,000 for Route B\nE. $80,000 for Route A and $40,000 for Route B\nF. $35,000 for Route A and $25,000 for Route B\nG. $70,000 for Route A and $35,000 for Route B\nH. $60,000 for Route A and $155,000 for Route B\nI. $90,000 for Route A and $155,000 for Route B\nJ. $120,000 for Route A and $75,000 for Route B\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Route A:  \n- Construction: 15 \u00d7 $6,000 = $90,000  \n- Taxes: 3% of $90,000 = $2,700  \n- Annual maintenance: 15 \u00d7 $2,000 = $30,000  \n- Total Year 1 cost: $90,000 (capital) + $2,700 (taxes) + $30,000 (maintenance) = $122,700 \u2014 but since only annual *costs* are compared, we consider recurring annual expenses plus tax and equivalent annual cost (EAC) of capital.  \n\nUsing EAC with 8% interest over 15 years:  \nEAC factor = i(1+i)^n / ((1+i)^n - 1) \u2248 0.1168  \nRoute A EAC: $90,000 \u00d7 0.1168 \u2248 $10,512  \nTaxes annually: $2,700  \nMaintenance: $30,000  \nTotal \u2248 $10,512 + $2,700 + $30,000 = $43,212 \u2192 closest to Option A\n\nRoute B:  \nLength: 10 miles (15 - 5 saved? Wait \u2014 Route B is 10 miles shorter? No \u2014 Route A is 15 miles, Route B is 10 miles (across lake)? Wait \u2014 \u201ccuts 5 miles across\u201d implies Route B is 10 miles? Unclear.\n\nWait: \"Route A is 15 miles... Route B ... cuts 5 miles across\" \u2014 likely Route B is 10 miles shorter? But says \"cuts 5 miles across\", probably meaning distance is 10 miles less? Or is it 5 miles long?\n\nRe-read: \"cuts 5 miles across the lake\" \u2014 so Route B is 5 miles long.\n\nSo Route B: 5 miles  \nConstruction: 5 \u00d7 $31,000 = $155,000  \nTaxes: 3% \u00d7 $155,000 = $4,650  \nAnnual maintenance: 5 \u00d7 $400 = $2,000  \nEAC: $155,000 \u00d7 0.1168 \u2248 $18,104  \nTotal annual cost: $18,104 + $4,650 + $2,000 \u2248 $24,754 \u2192 close to $23,654 in Option A\n\nBut $24,754 vs $23,654 \u2014 slight mismatch.\n\nWait \u2014 salvage value affects EAC.\n\nUse present value of salvage: $3,000 \u00d7 (P/F,8%,15) = $3,000 \u00d7 0.3152 \u2248 $945.6 per mile \u2192 total salvage PV = 15 \u00d7 $945.6 \u2248 $14,184  \nNet investment: $90,000 - $14,184 = $75,816  \nEAC: $75,816 \u00d7 0.1168 \u2248 $8,855  \n+ $30,000 maint + $2,700 tax = $41,555 \u2192 matches $41,558\n\nRoute B: Salvage = 5 \u00d7 $6,000 = $30,000  \nPV = $30,000 \u00d7 0.3152 = $9,456  \nNet investment: $155,000 - $9,456 = $145,544  \nEAC: $145,544 \u00d7 0.1168 \u2248 $16,999  \n+ $2,000 maint + $4,650 tax = $23,649 \u2248 $23,654\n\nMatches Option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
