    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, calculate the volume of one piece of lumber:  \n2 inches = 2/12 = 1/6 feet, 6 inches = 0.5 feet \u2192 Volume = (1/6) \u00d7 0.5 \u00d7 12 = 1 cubic foot per piece.  \n300 pieces = 300 board feet (since 1 board foot = 1/12 cubic foot, but here we convert properly: 1 board foot = 1 inch \u00d7 1 foot \u00d7 1 foot \u2192 so 1 cubic foot = 12 board feet).  \nThus, 300 \u00d7 12 = 3,600 board feet.  \nCost = (3,600 / 1,000) \u00d7 $140 = 3.6 \u00d7 140 = $504.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
