    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mr. Haskell has decided to buy a rental property. The building costs $50,000 and the land costs $30,000. The annual rent income is estimated to be $10,450 and the annual expense, $3,200. Mr. Haskell plans to depreciate the building by the straight line method over 40 years. Mr. Haskell wants to choose the best of three investment plans. Plan A Pay the full $80,000 from personal account. Plan B Borrow $30,000 and pay $50,000 from personal account. Rate of interest is 4(1/2)%. Plan C Borrow $60,000 and pay $20,000 from personal account. Rate of interest is 5 (1/4)%. If the tax rate is 40%, which investment plan has the highest rate of return?\n\nOptions: \nA. Plan B, if the interest rates drop to 3%\nB. Plan A, if the tax rate decreases to 30%\nC. Plan A\nD. Plan C, assuming rental income increases by 5% annually\nE. Plan C\nF. None of the plans\nG. Plan B\nH. Plan C, if additional tax deductions are available for interest paid\nI. Plan A, with a government grant covering 10% of the initial investment\nJ. Plan B, with an additional private investor contributing $10,000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the best plan, calculate after-tax cash flows and returns for each. Depreciation = $50,000 / 40 = $1,250/year. Net operating income = $10,450 - $3,200 = $7,250; taxable income = $7,250 - $1,250 = $6,000; tax = 40% \u00d7 $6,000 = $2,400; after-tax cash flow = $7,250 - $2,400 = $4,850.\n\nFor Plan A: Return = $4,850 / $80,000 = 6.06%.  \nPlan B: Interest = 4.5% \u00d7 $30,000 = $1,350; taxable income = $6,000 - $1,350 = $4,650; tax = $1,860; after-tax cash flow = $7,250 - $1,350 - $1,860 = $4,040; equity = $50,000; return = $4,040 / $50,000 = 8.08%.  \nPlan C: Interest = 5.25% \u00d7 $60,000 = $3,150; taxable income = $6,000 - $3,150 = $2,850; tax = $1,140; after-tax cash flow = $7,250 - $3,150 - $1,140 = $2,960; equity = $20,000; return = $2,960 / $20,000 = 14.8%.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
