      "generated_answer": "If standard time-series tools like ACF, PACF, and spectral analysis find no evidence of structure, it suggests the data lack autocorrelation and serial dependence. While this is consistent with independence, the most precise statistical implication is that the data are uncorrelated (zero autocorrelation at all lags), which is a weaker condition than independence but is directly what these tools assess. Independent data imply uncorrelatedness, but uncorrelatedness does not necessarily imply independence\u2014however, among the options, *uncorrelated* is the most directly supported by the absence of detectable structure in ACF/PACF/spectral analysis.\n\n$\\boxed{H}$",
