      "generated_answer": "The Constitution grants Congress the power to make rules for the governance and regulation of the armed forces under Article I, Section 8, which includes setting conditions on military activities such as joint exercises. While the President is Commander-in-Chief, Congress retains significant authority over military operations, especially those involving foreign engagements, through its legislative powers. Therefore, requiring advance notice for joint military exercises is a valid exercise of Congress\u2019s regulatory authority over the Armed Forces.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
