      "generated_answer": "The ordinance mandates that all waste within city limits\u2014regardless of origin\u2014must be processed locally before being shipped out, which may appear neutral on its face but effectively benefits local processing facilities by restricting out-of-state competition. Courts have previously ruled such laws unconstitutional under the dormant Commerce Clause when they favor in-state economic interests, even if applied uniformly. The requirement forces out-of-state processors to operate within the city, creating an undue burden on interstate commerce.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
