      "generated_answer": "The most persuasive argument is grounded in the Constitution's explicit grant of authority to Congress over the Supreme Court's appellate jurisdiction. Article III, Section 2, gives Congress the power to make \"exceptions\" and \"regulations\" concerning the appellate jurisdiction of the Supreme Court, which directly supports the statutory restriction. This textual basis makes option B the strongest constitutional argument.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
