    "global index": "AIME_0",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Quadratic polynomials $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ have leading coefficients $2$ and $-2,$ respectively. The graphs of both polynomials pass through the two points $(16,54)$ and $(20,53).$ Find $P(0) + Q(0).$\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $ P(x) = 2x^2 + ax + b $ and $ Q(x) = -2x^2 + cx + d $.  \nUsing $ P(16) = 54 $: $ 2(256) + 16a + b = 54 \\Rightarrow 512 + 16a + b = 54 \\Rightarrow 16a + b = -458 $.  \nUsing $ P(20) = 53 $: $ 2(400) + 20a + b = 53 \\Rightarrow 800 + 20a + b = 53 \\Rightarrow 20a + b = -747 $.  \nSubtracting: $ (20a + b) - (16a + b) = -747 - (-458) \\Rightarrow 4a = -289 \\Rightarrow a = -72.25 $.  \nThen $ 16(-72.25) + b = -458 \\Rightarrow -1156 + b = -458 \\Rightarrow b = 698 $. So $ P(0) = b = 698 $.  \nFor $ Q(x) $: $ -2(256) + 16c + d = 54 \\Rightarrow -512 + 16c + d = 54 \\Rightarrow 16c + d = 566 $.  \n$ -2(400) + 20c + d = 53 \\Rightarrow -800 + 20c + d = 53 \\Rightarrow 20c + d = 853 $.  \nSubtract: $ 4c = 287 \\Rightarrow c = 71.75 $, then $ 16(71.75) + d = 566 \\Rightarrow 1148 + d = 566 \\Rightarrow d = -582 $. So $ Q(0) = d = -582 $.  \nThus, $ P(0) + Q(0) = 698 + (-582) = 116 $.  \n\n\\boxed{{116}}",
      "success": true,
