    "global index": "AIME_15",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Adults made up $\\frac5{{12}}$ of the crowd of people at a concert. After a bus carrying $50$ more people arrived, adults made up $\\frac{{11}}{{25}}$ of the people at the concert. Find the minimum number of adults who could have been at the concert after the bus arrived.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $ x $ be the initial total number of people. Initially, adults are $ \\frac{5}{12}x $. After adding 50 people, total becomes $ x + 50 $, and adults become $ \\frac{11}{25}(x + 50) $. Assume the 50 new people include $ a $ adults; then:\n$$\n\\frac{5}{12}x + a = \\frac{11}{25}(x + 50)\n$$\nMultiply through by 300 (LCM of 12 and 25):\n$$\n125x + 300a = 132(x + 50) = 132x + 6600\n\\Rightarrow -7x + 300a = 6600\n\\Rightarrow 7x = 300a - 6600\n$$\nSo $ x = \\frac{300a - 6600}{7} $. We want smallest integer $ x > 0 $, and $ a $ integer between 0 and 50.\n\nTry small $ a $: $ a = 24 $ gives $ 300(24) = 7200 $, $ 7200 - 6600 = 600 $, $ x = 600 / 7 \\approx 85.7 $ \u2014 not integer. Try $ a = 25 $: $ 7500 - 6600 = 900 $, $ 900 / 7 \\not\\in \\mathbb{Z} $. $ a = 26 $: $ 7800 - 6600 = 1200 $, $ 1200/7 \\not\\in \\mathbb{Z} $. $ a = 30 $: $ 9000 - 6600 = 2400 $, $ 2400 / 7 \\approx 342.86 $. $ a = 32 $: $ 9600 - 6600 = 3000 $, $ 3000 / 7 \\not\\in \\mathbb{Z} $. $ a = 34 $: $ 10200 - 6600 = 3600 $, $ 3600 / 7 \\not\\in \\mathbb{Z} $. $ a = 37 $: $ 11100 - 6600 = 4500 $, $ 4500 / 7 \\not\\in \\mathbb{Z} $. $ a = 40 $: $ 12000 - 6600 = 5400 $, $ 5400 / 7 \\approx 771.4 $. $ a = 41 $: $ 12300 - 6600 = 5700 $, $ 5700 / 7 \\approx 814.3 $. $ a = 43 $: $ 12900 - 6600 = 6300 $, $ 6300 / 7 = 900 $. So $ x = 900 $, initial adults: $ \\frac{5}{12} \\cdot 900 = 375 $. New adults: $ 375 + 43 = 418 $. Total people now: $ 900 + 50 = 950 $. Check: $ \\frac{11}{25} \\cdot 950 = 418 $. Correct.\n\n\\boxed{418}",
