    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $ D, G, S, H $ represent the sets of people owning a diamond ring, golf clubs, garden spade, and candy hearts, respectively. Since all 900 residents own candy hearts, everyone is in $ H $. Let $ x $ be the number who own all four items. Using the principle of inclusion-exclusion for four sets and given data:  \nTotal = Sum of single owners - Sum of exactly two - 2\u00d7exactly three - 3\u00d7all four + ... but simplified via known counts:  \nWe know:  \n- Exactly two items: 437  \n- Exactly three items: 234  \nLet $ x $ be those with all four. Then the total number of people is:  \n$ 900 = (\\text{only one}) + 437 + 234 + x $.  \nSo those with only one item: $ 900 - 437 - 234 - x = 229 - x $.  \nNow sum over all ownerships: total item count = $ 195 + 367 + 562 + 900 = 2024 $.  \nEach person with exactly 1, 2, 3, 4 items contributes that many to total count:  \n$ 1(229 - x) + 2(437) + 3(234) + 4x = 2024 $  \nSolve: $ 229 - x + 874 + 702 + 4x = 2024 $ \u2192 $ 1805 + 3x = 2024 $ \u2192 $ 3x = 219 $ \u2192 $ x = 73 $.  \n\n\\boxed{{73}}",
