    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are $ n $ values of $ x $ in the interval $ 0 < x < 2\\pi $ where $ f(x) = \\sin(7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x)) = 0 $. For $ t $ of these $ n $ values of $ x $, the graph of $ y = f(x) $ is tangent to the $ x $-axis. Find $ n + t $.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We solve $ \\sin(7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x)) = 0 $. This implies $ 7\\pi \\cdot \\sin(5x) = k\\pi $ for integer $ k $, so $ \\sin(5x) = \\frac{k}{7} $. Since $ |\\sin(5x)| \\leq 1 $, $ k = -7, -6, \\dots, 7 $, but only $ k = -7 $ to $ 7 $ with $ |k| \\leq 7 $ and $ \\left|\\frac{k}{7}\\right| \\leq 1 $. So $ k = -7, -6, \\dots, 7 $: 15 values.\n\nFor each valid $ k $, $ \\sin(5x) = \\frac{k}{7} $ has 10 solutions in $ 0 < x < 2\\pi $ (since $ 5x $ spans $ 0 $ to $ 10\\pi $, and sine hits each value twice per period, 5 periods). But when $ \\left|\\frac{k}{7}\\right| = 1 $, i.e., $ k = \\pm7 $, $ \\sin(5x) = \\pm1 $, which occurs once per half-period \u2014 5 times each. So total $ n = 8 \\cdot 10 + 2 \\cdot 5 = 90 $.\n\nTangency occurs when $ f(x) = 0 $ and $ f'(x) = 0 $. $ f'(x) = \\cos(7\\pi \\sin(5x)) \\cdot 7\\pi \\cdot 5\\cos(5x) \\cdot \\cos(5x) $. At zeros, $ \\cos(7\\pi \\sin(5x)) = \\pm1 $, so $ f'(x) = 0 $ iff $ \\cos(5x) = 0 $. This happens when $ \\sin(5x) = \\pm1 $, i.e., $ k = \\pm7 $. Each gives 5 solutions, so $ t = 10 $.\n\nThus, $ n + t = 90 + 10 = \\boxed{100} $.",
