    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the full fare be $ F $ and the reservation charge be $ R $. Then, $ F + R = 216 $. Also, one full and one half ticket cost: $ F + R + \\frac{F}{2} + R = 327 $, which simplifies to $ \\frac{3F}{2} + 2R = 327 $. Solving: multiply first equation by 2: $ 2F + 2R = 432 $; subtract second: $ 2F + 2R - (\\frac{3F}{2} + 2R) = 432 - 327 $ \u2192 $ \\frac{F}{2} = 105 $ \u2192 $ F = 210 $. Then $ R = 216 - 210 = 6 $.\n\n\\boxed{{210}}, \\boxed{{6}}",
