    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the fraction be $\\frac{x}{y}$.  \nGiven: $\\frac{x+1}{y+1} = \\frac{4}{5}$ \u2192 $5(x+1) = 4(y+1)$ \u2192 $5x + 5 = 4y + 4$ \u2192 $5x - 4y = -1$.  \nAlso: $\\frac{x-5}{y-5} = \\frac{1}{2}$ \u2192 $2(x-5) = y-5$ \u2192 $2x - 10 = y - 5$ \u2192 $2x - y = 5$.  \nSolving: From second equation, $y = 2x - 5$. Substitute into first: $5x - 4(2x - 5) = -1$ \u2192 $5x - 8x + 20 = -1$ \u2192 $-3x = -21$ \u2192 $x = 7$, so $y = 9$.  \n\n\\boxed{\\dfrac{7}{9}}",
