      "generated_answer": "We are given:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = 2, \\quad \\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\nLet $ \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix} $. Then:\n\n1. Dot product:  \n$$\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = 1x + 1y + 1z = x + y + z = 2\n$$\n\n2. Cross product:  \n$$\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n1 & 1 & 1 \\\\\nx & y & z\n\\end{vmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n1\\cdot z - 1\\cdot y \\\\\n1\\cdot x - 1\\cdot z \\\\\n1\\cdot y - 1\\cdot x\n\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\nz - y \\\\\nx - z \\\\\ny - x\n\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\nSet equal to $ \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} $:\n\n$$\nz - y = 1 \\quad (1), \\quad x - z = -2 \\quad (2), \\quad y - x = 1 \\quad (3)\n$$\n\nFrom (1): $ z = y + 1 $  \nFrom (2): $ x = z - 2 = (y + 1) - 2 = y - 1 $  \nFrom (3): $ y - x = y - (y - 1) = 1 $ \u2713\n\nNow use $ x + y + z = 2 $:\n\n$$\n(y - 1) + y + (y + 1) = 3y = 2 \\Rightarrow y = \\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nThen:  \n$ x = y - 1 = -\\frac{1}{3} $,  \n$ z = y + 1 = \\frac{5}{3} $\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3} \\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -\\dfrac{1}{3} \\\\ \\dfrac{2}{3} \\\\ \\dfrac{5}{3} \\end{pmatrix}}",
