    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We compute $10! = 10 \\times 9 \\times 8 \\times \\cdots \\times 1 = 3628800$. The prime factorization of $10!$ is $2^8 \\cdot 3^4 \\cdot 5^2 \\cdot 7^1$. For $x^3$ to divide $10!$, each exponent in the prime factorization of $x^3$ must be at most the corresponding exponent in $10!$, and divisible by 3.\n\nSo if $x = 2^a \\cdot 3^b \\cdot 5^c \\cdot 7^d$, then $3a \\leq 8$, $3b \\leq 4$, $3c \\leq 2$, $3d \\leq 1$. Thus:  \n$a = 0,1,2$ \u2192 3 choices;  \n$b = 0,1$ \u2192 2 choices;  \n$c = 0$ \u2192 1 choice;  \n$d = 0$ \u2192 1 choice.  \n\nTotal: $3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 = 6$.\n\n\\boxed{{6}}",
