      "generated_answer": "We apply Stokes\u2019 Theorem: $\\int_C \\mathbf{F} \\cdot d\\mathbf{r} = \\iint_S (\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}) \\cdot d\\mathbf{S}$. Compute $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F} = (-y, -z, -x)$. The surface $S$ is the plane $x + y + z = 1$ over the triangle; unit normal $\\mathbf{n} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(1,1,1)$. Then $(\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}) \\cdot \\mathbf{n} = -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(x+y+z) = -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ on $S$. The area of the triangle is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$, so flux is $-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = -\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
