      "generated_answer": "The function $ f(x, y) = 1 - x - y $ when $ x + y \\leq 1 $, and 0 otherwise, over $[0,1] \\times [0,1]$. The region where $ x + y \\leq 1 $ is a triangle with vertices at $(0,0), (1,0), (0,1)$, area $ \\frac{1}{2} $. Integrate $ 1 - x - y $ over this triangle:\n\n$$\n\\int_0^1 \\int_0^{1-x} (1 - x - y)\\,dy\\,dx = \\int_0^1 \\left[(1-x)y - \\frac{y^2}{2}\\right]_0^{1-x} dx = \\int_0^1 \\frac{(1-x)^2}{2} dx = \\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nBut wait \u2014 recheck: $ \\int_0^1 \\frac{(1-x)^2}{2} dx = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{6} \\approx 0.16667 $\n\n\\boxed{H}",
