      "generated_answer": "We analyze $ g(x) = \\lim_{r \\to 0} \\left( (x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1} \\right)^{1/r} $. Using asymptotic expansion for small $ r $, $ (x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1} \\approx x^{r+1} \\left( \\frac{r+1}{x} + o(1/x) \\right) $, leading to logarithmic analysis. After simplification, $ \\ln g(x) \\sim \\ln x + \\ln(1 + 1/x) \\cdot \\frac{1}{r} $, but more careful computation shows $ g(x) \\sim x \\cdot e $. Thus, $ g(x)/x \\to e \\approx 2.7182818 $.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
