    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose $E \\subset(0,2 \\pi) is a measurable set. \\left\\{{\\xi_n\night\\}}$ is an arbitrary sequence of real numbers. If the Lebesgue measure of E is 2, what is $\\lim _{{n \nightarrow \\infty}} \\int_E \\cos ^2 (n x+\\xi_n ) dx$? Return the numeric.\n\nOptions: \nA. $\\frac{{\\sqrt{{2}}{{2}}$\nB. 0.0\nC. $\\pi$\nD. 1.5\nE. 1.0\nF. 3.0\nG. 2.0\nH. 2.5\nI. 0.5\nJ. $\\frac{{\\pi}}{{2}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
