      "generated_answer": "The integral of $\\cos^2(nx + \\xi_n)$ over a measurable set $E$ with Lebesgue measure 2 can be rewritten using the identity $\\cos^2\\theta = \\frac{1 + \\cos(2\\theta)}{2}$. Then, $\\int_E \\cos^2(nx + \\xi_n)\\,dx = \\frac{1}{2}|E| + \\frac{1}{2}\\int_E \\cos(2nx + 2\\xi_n)\\,dx$. As $n \\to \\infty$, the oscillatory term $\\int_E \\cos(2nx + 2\\xi_n)\\,dx \\to 0$ by the Riemann-Lebesgue Lemma. Thus, the limit is $\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 = 1.0$.\n\n$\\boxed{E}$",
