      "generated_answer": "The product of five dice rolls is not composite only if it is 1 (all ones) or a prime number. The only way to get a prime is if four dice show 1 and one die shows a prime (2, 3, or 5), giving 5 \u00d7 3 = 15 such outcomes. Total outcomes are $6^5 = 7776$, so non-composite outcomes are $1 + 15 = 16$, making composite probability $1 - \\frac{16}{7776} = \\frac{7760}{7776}$, but this isn't listed. Wait \u2014 question asks for probability it *is* composite. Only $\\frac{485}{486}$ is close to 1. But $ \\frac{485}{486} \\approx 0.9979 $, and $1 - \\frac{16}{7776} = \\frac{7760}{7776} = \\frac{485}{486}$. So correct.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
