      "generated_answer": "The coefficient of performance (COP) for a reversible refrigerator is given by $ \\text{COP} = \\frac{T_c}{T_h - T_c} $, where temperatures must be in Kelvin. Converting the temperatures: refrigerator $ T_c = 275.4\\,\\text{K} $, freezer $ T_c = 255.4\\,\\text{K} $, room $ T_h = 291.5\\,\\text{K} $. Calculating COPs: COP_refrigerator \u2248 17.0, COP_freezer \u2248 7.0, so the cost ratio is $ \\frac{17.0}{7.0} \\approx 2.4 $.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
