    "global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8853",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A barge of mass 15,000 kg, made from metal of density 7500 kg\\bulletm^-3, is being loaded in a closed dock of sur-face area 6633 m^2 with ore of density 3 g\\bulletcm^-3. When 80,000 kg of ore are aboard, the barge sinks. How does the water level in the dock alter? The area of the barge is assumed negligible in comparison with the area of the dock.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.5 cm\nB. 2 cm\nC. 0.2 cm\nD. 2.5 cm\nE. 0.8 cm\nF. 1.5 cm\nG. 3 cm\nH. 1 cm\nI. 0.5 cm\nJ. 4 cm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The barge displaces an amount of water equal to the combined weight of the barge and the ore before sinking. Once it sinks, the volume of water displaced equals the volume of the submerged barge and ore. The change in water level is determined by dividing the total additional displaced volume by the dock's surface area.\n\nVolume of barge = 15,000 / 7500 = 2 m\u00b3; Volume of ore = 80,000 kg / 3000 kg/m\u00b3 = 26.67 m\u00b3; Total volume added after sinking = 2 + 26.67 = 28.67 m\u00b3. Water level rise = 28.67 / 6633 \u2248 0.00432 m = 4.32 cm. However, before sinking, the barge already displaced (15,000 + 80,000) / 1000 = 95 m\u00b3 of water due to floating. After sinking, only 28.67 m\u00b3 is displaced, so the displaced volume decreases by 95 - 28.67 = 66.33 m\u00b3. Thus, water level drops by 66.33 / 6633 \u2248 0.01 m = 1 cm.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 289,
        "output_tokens": 302,
        "total_tokens": 591
