    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The charge density \u03c1 = ar implies increasing charge with radius inside the sphere (r < R). For r < R, integrating gives enclosed charge proportional to r\u2074, so electric field E \u221d r\u00b2 \u2014 increasing non-linearly. For r > R, total charge is fixed, so E \u221d 1/r\u00b2 \u2014 decreasing, not constant or increasing.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{F}",
