    "global index": "MathQA_1611",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a cistern of capacity 8000 litres measures externally 3.3 m by 2.6 m by 1.4 m and its walls are 5 cm thick . the thickness of the bottom is :\n\nOptions: \nA. 90 cm\nB. 4 dm\nC. 1 m\nD. 1.1 cm\nE. none of these\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The external dimensions are 3.3 m \u00d7 2.6 m \u00d7 1.4 m, and wall thickness is 5 cm (0.05 m), so internal length and breadth are reduced by 2\u00d70.05 m = 0.1 m. Thus, internal dimensions: length = 3.2 m, breadth = 2.5 m. Let the bottom thickness be $ x $ meters; then internal height = $ 1.4 - x $. Internal volume = $ 3.2 \u00d7 2.5 \u00d7 (1.4 - x) = 8 \u00d7 (1.4 - x) $ m\u00b3 = $ 8000(1.4 - x) $ liters. Set equal to 8000 liters: $ 8000(1.4 - x) = 8000 $ \u2192 $ 1.4 - x = 1 $ \u2192 $ x = 0.4 $ m = 40 cm = 4 dm.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
