      "generated_answer": "The pressure increases linearly from 15 psi at the surface to 30 psi at 33 feet, so the rate is (30 - 15) / 33 = 0.4545 psi per foot. To find the depth at which pressure reaches 25,000 psi, solve: 15 + 0.4545d = 25,000 \u2192 d \u2248 (25,000 - 15) / 0.4545 \u2248 54,972 feet. This depth is closest to option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
