    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: the smallest value of n , for which 2 n + 1 is not a prime number is\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 4\nC. 5\nD. 6\nE. 7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We test values of $ n $ starting from 1 upward to find the smallest $ n $ such that $ 2n + 1 $ is not prime.\n\nFor $ n = 1 $: $ 2(1) + 1 = 3 $ (prime)  \n$ n = 2 $: $ 5 $ (prime)  \n$ n = 3 $: $ 7 $ (prime)  \n$ n = 4 $: $ 9 = 3 \\times 3 $ (not prime)\n\nThus, the smallest $ n $ for which $ 2n + 1 $ is not prime is 4.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
