    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The volume of the wire is given as 55 cm\u00b3. The wire is cylindrical with a diameter of 1 mm, so radius = 0.5 mm = 0.05 cm. Using the formula for volume of a cylinder, $ V = \\pi r^2 h $, we solve for length $ h $:  \n$ 55 = \\pi (0.05)^2 h $ \u2192 $ h = \\frac{55}{\\pi \\times 0.0025} \\approx \\frac{55}{0.00785} \\approx 7000 $ cm = 70 m.  \n\nThus, the length of the wire is 70 metres.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
