    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: suzie \u2019 s discount footwear sells all pairs of shoes for one price and all pairs of boots for another price . on monday the store sold 22 pairs of shoes and 16 pairs of boots for $ 540 . on tuesday the store sold 8 pairs of shoes and 32 pairs of boots for $ 720 . how much more do pairs of boots cost than pairs of shoes at suzie \u2019 s discount footwear ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 12\nB. 11\nC. 10\nD. 15\nE. 16\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let \\( s \\) be the price of shoes and \\( b \\) be the price of boots. From the problem, we have:  \n\\( 22s + 16b = 540 \\) and \\( 8s + 32b = 720 \\).  \nSolving these equations gives \\( s = 10 \\) and \\( b = 20 \\), so boots cost $10 more than shoes.  \n\n\\boxed{C}",
