  {
    "global index": "MathQA_1373",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: the average expenditure of a labourer for 10 months was 85 and he fell into debt . in the next 4 months by reducing his monthly expenses to 60 he not only cleared off his debt but also saved 30 . his monthly income is\n\nOptions: \nA. 180\nB. 100\nC. 112\nD. 110\nE. none of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The total expenditure for 10 months at $85$ per month is $850$. Let monthly income be $x$. Total income in 14 months is $14x$. In the next 4 months, he spends $60$ per month, so expenditure is $240$, and he saves $30$, meaning income exceeds expenditure by $30$. So, total income = total expenditure + savings: $14x = 850 + 240 - \\text{debt} + 30$. But since he cleared the debt and saved $30$, the deficit from first 10 months ($10(x - 85)$) must equal the surplus in next 4 months ($4(60 - x) + 30$). Solving: $10x - 850 = (240 - 4x) + 30$ \u2192 $10x - 850 = 270 - 4x$ \u2192 $14x = 1120$ \u2192 $x = 80$. But this contradicts; rechecking: better equation: total income = $14x$, total spending = $850 + 240 = 1090$, and he saved $30$, so $14x = 1090 + 30 = 1120$, so $x = 80$. But that can't be as he spent $85$ and went into debt \u2014 income must be less than $85$. Wait: if he spent $85$ monthly for 10 months, total outflow $850$, income $10x$, so debt = $850 - 10x$. Then next 4 months, income $4x$, expense $240$, saving $30$, so $4x - 240 = 30$ \u2192 $4x = 270$ \u2192 $x = 67.5$. Then debt = $850 - 675 = 175$, but saving only $30$, not enough. Mistake: saving $30$ after clearing debt. So $4x - 240 = 30 + (850 - 10x)$. Then $4x - 240 = 880 - 10x$ \u2192 $14x = 1120$ \u2192 $x = 80$. Then debt = $850 - 800 = 50$, surplus = $4\u00d780 - 240 = 80$, so $50$ clears debt, $30$ saved. Correct. Monthly income $80$, not in options. So answer is E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
