    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a circle in the coordinate plane passes through points ( - 3 , - 2 ) and ( 1 , - 4 ) . what is the smallest possible area of that circle ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 13 \u03c0\nB. 26 \u03c0\nC. 262 \u221a \u03c0\nD. 5 \u03c0\nE. 64 \u03c0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The smallest possible circle passing through two points has those points as endpoints of a diameter. The distance between (\u22123, \u22122) and (1, \u22124) is \u221a[(1 + 3)\u00b2 + (\u22124 + 2)\u00b2] = \u221a(16 + 4) = \u221a20 = 2\u221a5. Thus, the radius is \u221a5, and the area is \u03c0(\u221a5)\u00b2 = 5\u03c0.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
