  {
    "global index": "MathQA_518",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if f ( f ( n ) ) + f ( n ) = 2 n + 3 and f ( 0 ) = 1 , what is the value of f ( 2012 ) ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 222\nB. 2787\nC. 2013\nD. 2778\nE. 10222\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given the functional equation:\n\n$$\nf(f(n)) + f(n) = 2n + 3\n$$\nand initial condition:\n$$\nf(0) = 1\n$$\n\nLet\u2019s try to compute small values.  \nSet $ n = 0 $:  \n$$\nf(f(0)) + f(0) = 3 \\Rightarrow f(1) + 1 = 3 \\Rightarrow f(1) = 2\n$$\n\nNow $ n = 1 $:  \n$$\nf(f(1)) + f(1) = 2(1) + 3 = 5 \\Rightarrow f(2) + 2 = 5 \\Rightarrow f(2) = 3\n$$\n\n$ n = 2 $:  \n$$\nf(3) + 3 = 7 \\Rightarrow f(3) = 4\n$$\n\n$ n = 3 $:  \n$$\nf(4) + 4 = 9 \\Rightarrow f(4) = 5\n$$\n\nIt appears that $ f(n) = n + 1 $. Let's test this hypothesis.\n\nAssume $ f(n) = n + 1 $. Then:\n$$\nf(f(n)) = f(n+1) = n + 2\n$$\nSo:\n$$\nf(f(n)) + f(n) = (n+2) + (n+1) = 2n + 3\n$$\nWhich matches the equation. Also $ f(0) = 1 $, so it satisfies the initial condition.\n\nThus, $ f(n) = n + 1 $ is the solution.\n\nTherefore, $ f(2012) = 2013 $\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 191,
        "output_tokens": 370,
        "total_tokens": 561
      },
      "provider": "local-vllm",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 0.00018357000000000003,
