      "generated_answer": "The Debye\u2013H\u00fcckel equation relates the logarithm of the activity coefficient to the ionic strength and other parameters. The log of the activity coefficient is proportional to the inverse of the dielectric constant raised to the 3/2 power, but more directly, it is proportional to the charge number and the square root of ionic strength. However, the parameter referred to here is the Bjerrum length, which depends on temperature and solvent properties, but the most common and direct answer is the ionic strength itself, though the proportionality involves the square root of ionic strength. The parameter being asked for, whose negative three-halves power appears, is typically the dielectric constant.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{dielectric constant}}",
